<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">UNDERSTANDING OUR SERVICE</span><h1>Terms and Conditions</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 16 October 2026</p><p>These terms apply to <strong>atscvdetector.com</strong>, owned and operated by <strong>Code Dev Solutions, Zimbabwe</strong> (“we”, “us” or “our”). “You” means the person using atscvdetector. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. Agreement and related policies</h2><p>Read these terms before creating an account or requesting a service. By taking either action, you agree to these terms. If you disagree, do not create an account or request a service. Our <a href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a> explains personal information processing, and our <a href="{{ route('refund') }}">Refund Policy</a> explains payment remedies. Nothing here removes rights that applicable law does not allow us to exclude.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. Our services</h2><p>atscvdetector provides digital CV and resume tools: CV building, document import and export, comparison with job descriptions, formatting assistance and optional AI-assisted rewriting. Access depends on feature availability, account requirements and the limits shown in the service. Upcoming features are not a promise of immediate availability.</p><p>We help you prepare and assess career documents. We are not an employer, recruitment agency, placement service, immigration adviser or an employer's Applicant Tracking System. These tools do not submit applications or contact employers for you.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. ATS estimates and employment outcomes</h2><p>A match score estimates textual alignment between your CV and the supplied job description. It is not an employer's ATS score, a certification, an assessment of your fitness for a role or a hiring decision. Employers use different systems, screening questions and selection criteria that may be unknown to us.</p><p>“ATS-friendly” describes an effort to improve readable structure and relevant wording. We do not guarantee compatibility with every ATS, a particular score, an interview, an offer, a salary, a visa or employment. A higher score does not necessarily mean a stronger application.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Eligibility and account security</h2><p>You must be at least 18 and able to enter a binding agreement to create an account. Supply accurate account information, keep credentials secure and report suspected unauthorised access promptly. Do not impersonate another person or share access to evade service limits. If you choose Google sign-in, Google's own account terms also apply.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Your content and responsibilities</h2><p>Submit only material you own or are authorised to use. Have a lawful basis for including another person's information, such as referee details. Remove unnecessary identity numbers, financial details, medical information and other sensitive data.</p><p>Keep your CV truthful. Review names, contact details, dates, qualifications, skills and achievements before downloading or applying. You decide which suggestions to accept and remain responsible for the application you submit. Keep your own copies of important documents.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. AI and document conversion</h2><p>Optional AI tools use an external service provider to process submitted content. Generated wording can contain errors, omissions, unsupported claims or unsuitable language. Treat it as a draft, not verified fact or professional advice. Do not accept invented experience, qualifications or results.</p><p>Imports and exports may change formatting, omit text or misidentify fields. Scans and complex layouts may not be readable. Inspect the editor and the final file, including page breaks and content order. Any processing-time estimate depends on the document, network and external services and is not a guaranteed delivery time.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Acceptable use</h2><p>Do not use the service for fraud, unlawful discrimination, harassment, infringement, malware or unauthorised disclosure of personal data. Do not bypass account controls, access other people's records, overload the service or automate requests to evade limits. Report security concerns through support without accessing or copying another user's information.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Plans, prices and payment</h2><p>Available plans and payment methods are shown at checkout. Creating an account or viewing a plan does not authorise a charge. Free accounts receive 15 welcome credits once. Analysis costs 5 credits and a CV revamp costs 10 credits; manual editing and downloads use no credits. Subscription credits reset monthly during the paid term; purchased top-up credits carry over. Annual plans are paid yearly with credits allocated monthly.</p><p>Before payment, the order screen shows the service, total price, currency, applicable taxes and fees, delivery details and any renewal or cancellation terms. Recurring billing requires clear disclosure and your agreement. Our Refund Policy applies to purchases accepted by Code Dev Solutions for accepted purchases.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>9. Ownership and permission to process</h2><p>You retain your rights in content you submit. You give us limited permission to store, reproduce, convert and process it, including through necessary providers, to deliver your requested features, secure the service and comply with law. This permission does not authorise selling your CV or publishing it as a testimonial. Retention and disclosure are explained in the Privacy Policy.</p><p>You may use your generated CV for lawful purposes, subject to existing third-party rights. AI output may not be unique and exclusive intellectual property rights in it are not guaranteed. Our original software, branding, designs and written site content belong to Code Dev Solutions or their licensors. Third-party materials retain their respective rights.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>10. Availability, suspension and closure</h2><p>Maintenance, faults and external outages can interrupt service. We may change features or reasonable usage limits, without removing remedies for services already purchased. We may restrict access when reasonably necessary to address abuse, security risks or a breach of these terms. Where appropriate, we will explain the restriction and allow you to contact support; urgent legal or security circumstances may require immediate action.</p><p>You may stop using the service and request account deletion. Account restrictions do not automatically remove refund or consumer rights. Back up your documents before closing your account.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>11. Service standards and liability</h2><p>We will exercise reasonable care and skill, subject to any stronger standard required by law. Beyond express commitments and mandatory rights, we do not promise uninterrupted operation, error-free outputs or fitness for every personal purpose.</p><p>To the extent permitted by law, we are not responsible for indirect or consequential losses, lost employment opportunities or independent employer decisions. This does not exclude a remedy merely because AI was involved, or exclude liability for fraud, deliberate misconduct, gross negligence or anything that cannot lawfully be limited. Mandatory consumer protections prevail over conflicting wording here.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>12. Questions, complaints and disputes</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with your account email, a description of the issue and any order reference. Never send passwords or full payment credentials. We aim to acknowledge complaints within five business days and provide an outcome or progress update within fourteen business days. These targets do not restrict your rights.</p><p>Zimbabwean law governs these terms, subject to mandatory protections applying to you elsewhere. Disputes may be brought before a court with lawful jurisdiction. We do not require compulsory private arbitration or waiver of access to courts, regulators or payment-provider dispute procedures. Where appropriate, you may approach the <a href="https://cpc.org.zw/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Consumer Protection Commission of Zimbabwe (opens in a new tab)</a>.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>13. Updates and interpretation</h2><p>We will date revised terms and give reasonable notice of material changes through the site or account communications where appropriate. Changes apply prospectively and do not retrospectively remove purchase rights. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining terms continue insofar as law permits. Delayed enforcement is not a waiver.</p><p>For an explanation of any clause before requesting a service, contact Code Dev Solutions at <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>.</p></section>
